{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And a bull and a ram for peace-offerings.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Torat Kohanim: Why did Israel offer two — a calf and a bull? Because the worship was likened to two species, as it is said, ״עשו להם עגל מסכה״, and elsewhere it says (Psalms 106:20): ״וימירו את כבודם בתבנית שור״. Let a bull come and atone for the deed of the bull; let a calf come and atone for the deed of the calf. You shall know that the Place was appeased to atone for your iniquities — the transgression you fear has already been slaughtered before the Place, as it is said: ״לזבוח לפני ה׳״." "<b>For today YHWH will appear to you.</b> It should have said נראה with a segol, for thus the language: נראה with a segol for the masculine, and נראה with a qamatz for the feminine. And from this it is possible to say, by way of the Kabbalah, that it is as a participle standing in the feminine, and it is an allusion to the attribute of Judgment, which appeared on that day, as it is written (Leviticus 9): ״וירא כבוד ה׳ אל כל העם״, and because of this it used the language נראה — and it is like the language of (Psalms 130:3): ״אם עונות תשמר יה״, which is not direct but feminine and hidden language. And you already know the matter of what is written (Exodus 24:17): ״ומראה כבוד ה׳ כאש אוכלת״, and this is what it says: ״זה הדבר אשר צוה ה׳ תעשו וירא אליכם כבוד ה׳״ — it would have been sufficient to say ״אשר צוה ה׳ תעשו וירא אליכם״, and the word וירא refers back to YHWH; but it added to say ״כבוד ה׳״ in order to explain concerning the commandment, blessed be He, and concerning the Glory that appeared."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:17.564230109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}